Great question! Knowing the origin of a log message (the file and possibly the line number) significantly improves debugging, especially in larger projects.

Here are several approaches and suggestions to enhance your logger utility to include file and line info automatically:
1. Use Error().stack to capture call site info

You can create a helper function that captures the stack trace, parses it, and extracts the caller file and line number. This way, your logger can prepend this info to each log message automatically.

