"
When You Might Not Need ActiveForm or a Form Model for the Cart

    If the cart data is manipulated mostly via AJAX requests or buttons (e.g., “Add to cart” buttons), you often don’t need a formal form model — just simple request parameters like product ID and quantity.
    The cart itself is often stored in session, cookies, database, or cache — and is mostly managed server-side as a component or service rather than a form object.
    In such cases, your Cart is better represented by a dedicated class or component (e.g., CartService, CartComponent) that handles add/remove items, update quantities, persist the cart state, calculate totals, etc.
