is it possible to have yii2 debug tool ignore folders? and file names?

Yes, in Yii2 Debug tool it is possible to exclude certain folders or filenames from being traced or shown in the debug output, although it is not provided as a simple configuration option out-of-the-box. You need to customize the Debug Module or its panels such as the TimelinePanel or the LoggerPanel.
Overview

The Yii2 Debug tool collects stack traces and logs, showing files involved in requests. The file paths shown come from trace information. If you want the debugger to ignore trace entries from certain folders (like vendor/ or runtime/ or specific files), you can customize the panels that collect trace data by filtering out these entries.
Approaches to ignore folders/files
1. Customize the Debug Panels (e.g. TimelinePanel)

The yii\debug\panels\TimelinePanel gathers profiling data (including stack traces). You can extend this panel, override methods like save() or getTimeline() to filter out traces originating from specified folders or files.

Example:

namespace app\debug;

use yii\debug\panels\TimelinePanel;

class CustomTimelinePanel extends TimelinePanel
{
    public function save()
    {
        $data = parent::save();

        // Filter timeline events, remove events from specific folders/files
        $filteredEvents = [];
        foreach ($data['messages'] as $event) {
            if (isset($event[2]['file'])) {
                $file = $event[2]['file'];
                // Exclude vendor directory or runtime folder
                if (strpos($file, '/vendor/') !== false || strpos($file, '/runtime/') !== false) {
                    continue; // skip adding this event
                }
                // Exclude specific filename example
                if (basename($file) === 'SomeFileToIgnore.php') {
                    continue;
                }
            }
            $filteredEvents[] = $event;
        }

        $data['messages'] = $filteredEvents;

        return $data;
